 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Invariance under universal homeomorphisms",
 "statement": "Let $u\\colon Z'\\to Z$ be a universal homeomorphism. Then\n$\\mathcal G\\in\\shv{\\et Z}$ is constant (locally constant) if and only if\n$u^*\\mathcal G$ is. If moreover $u$ is a surjective closed immersion, then\n$\\mathcal G$ is finite (finite locally constant) if and only if\n$u^*\\mathcal G$ is.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-p1/lemma-constructible-universal-homeomorphism-invariance.md",
  "place": "node lemma-constructible-universal-homeomorphism-invariance, order 1168",
  "external": [
